error[E0403]: `window` of `psd` is a duration written out, such as `2 s` or `500ms`
 --> spectrum.tsl:5:18
  |
5 | out s1 = a | psd(long)
  |                  ^^^^
  |
  = note: it fixes the shape of the graph, so it cannot be a param or be computed

error[E0403]: `window` of `psd` is too short for a spectrum
 --> spectrum.tsl:6:14
  |
6 | out s2 = a | psd(20 ms)
  |              ^^^^^^^^^^ 20 samples at 1 kHz
  |
  = help: a spectrum takes at least 60 samples

error[E0413]: `lowpass` works on a signal in time, and this is a spectrum
  --> spectrum.tsl:11:10
   |
11 | out s3 = spectrum | lowpass(10 Hz)
   |          ^^^^^^^^ the spectrum of /0/field
   |
   = help: apply it before `psd`

error[E0413]: cannot subtract signals in different rate domains
  --> spectrum.tsl:12:21
   |
12 | out s4 = spectrum - a
   |          -------- 255 bins of 1.953125 Hz (from the spectrum of /0/field)
   |                     ^ 1 kHz (from /0/field)
   |
   = note: signals in different domains share no sample instants, even at
           the same rate
   = help: bring them into one domain first, with `align(…)`
